     {"@type":"Question","name":"How does AIdeazz keep AI agents from dying silently?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Every product declares a health check, a restart command and a PM2 or systemd process name in a single resilience config. A watchdog polls those checks and restarts a dead process, and failures surface in Telegram rather than waiting to be noticed. Silent death was the original failure mode, so a service that stops answering is treated as an incident, not a gap in the graph."}},
